       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for oral ibuprofen in adults.\n\n- **Daily limit:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under supervision. Over-the-counter labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single-dose limit:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. A 1600 mg dose is above that.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, which may be where the number came from, given as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg four times daily really is intended, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note flagging it as above the usual maximum. A pharmacist will probably need to verify it."
      }
